1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham Drach lived in the mid17th century in
2 CONT Frankfort. He was the most prominent member of
2 CONT the Drach family, one of the richest and most respected
2 CONT Frankfurt Jewish families. Isidor Kracauer,
2 CONT the chronicler of the Frankfurt Jews, described him
2 CONT as follows: “His breadth of vision, his commercial
2 CONT talent and ability to make best use of favorable
2 CONT times, his skill in handling people and issues, and
2 CONT not least his punctilious honesty with its absolute
2 CONT rejection of any unfair profit gained him the absolute
2 CONT confidence of high and low alike in both Jewish
2 CONT and Christian society. His name was highly valued on the Amsterdam and Hamburg exchanges
2 CONT and at the courts of many neighboring princes whose financial needs he supplied as their court
2 CONT factor.”
2 CONT Drach was frequently given important commissions by the Jewish community and was elected to its
2 CONT highest offices as “master builder” and treasurer. He was appointed plenipotentiary on behalf of the
2 CONT Frankfurt Jews in important negotiations at the imperial court in Vienna, he passed away in and died
2 CONT in 1687. (From http://judengasse.de/ehtml/P009.htm.)
2 CONT
