1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Act #476 [English Translation]: 17.08.1640, page 234: Christofle Mercier (?), clerk of the bank of Cheminot, owes Nathan Cahen, a Jew living in Raimport, the sum of 360 francs; the receipt in the margin, dated 12.1
2 CONC 2.1641, is made by Magdelaine Levy, wife of the said Nathan Cahen "iceluy presently in Frankfurt for about ten months"; she signs in Hebrew: "Mindlen Levi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Act #796 [English Translation]: 04.02.1682, folio 18: Judas LEVY and Natan CAHEIN his son-in-law; Judas signs in Hebrew "Yehuda bar Eliezer" while Nathan simply signs his first and last name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Metz Memorbuch #428 [English Translation]: "Rabbi Nathan, son of Rabbi Ouri Cahen, who for more than forty years mortified himself by fasting, and for more than twenty years mortified himself by fasting from one Sabbath to another
2 CONC ... His heirs made a donation to the hospice for him". Died on Wednesday evening and buried on Thursday, the second day of Shavuot 5446 [30 May 1686]
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustini p. 288
