1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Metz Memorbuch Entry #248 [English Translation]: The righteous Rabbi Gerson son of Rabbi Ouri... Aaron, for he studied the Law day and night to train many students. He was hospitable and humble in all his actions. 
2 CONC He blew the shofar on Rosh Hashanah and often made public offerings in a pleasant way and with great fervor. He was for a long time in charge of the charity box, and for twenty-five years he was in charge of the candles of the lig
2 CONC ht behind the officiant in the synagogue. His wife and children made a donation to the hospice for him. He died on Wednesday and was buried on Thursday, 7 Elul 5424 (28 Aug 1664)  
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 288 Faustini
2 CONT
2 CONT né entre 1580 et 1585 à Oettingen selon GenAmi 69 p. 18?
