1 NAME Joseph /Goldschmidt / Hameln/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 _MARNM Goldschmidt / Hameln
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1686
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lemgo
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1736 AND 1738
2 ADDR
3 CITY Detmold
3 CTRY Germany
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1712 Samuel Goldschmidt obtained a letter of protection (Geleitbrief) for his son Joseph in Lemgo. In 1720 Joseph and his brother Isaak Goldschmidt were appointed as Court Jews in Lippe-Detmold. In 1729 they cea
2 CONC sed to be Court Jews (source: Heinrich Schnee, Die Hoffinanz und der Moderne Staat, Volume III (Berlin: Duncker & Humblot, 1955), p. 94).
2 CONT
2 CONT The archives of Lemgo and Lippe mention Joseph in Lemgo from 1708 (Lemgo A 7315) to 1736 (Lippe 8 G 148). In 1738 they mention his heirs (Lemgo A 7317). Thus, he was born in or before ca. 1693 (=1708-15).
1 FAMC @F6000000002803288587@
1 FAMS @F6000000002803288578@
1 RFN geni:6000000002802359321
1 SUBM @S6000000002764082210@
1 OBJE
