1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the widow of Isak Bondi.  SeeTobias Jakobovits,  Die Verbindung der Prager Familien Oettingen-Spira (Wedeles)-Bondi.
2 CONT
2 CONT I do beleive that the following [copied from David Oppenheim's profile] fits the personal data: Oppenheim subsequently moved from Nikolsburg to Prague, where he took up the post of chief rabbi in 1702. His wife died in 1712, and h
2 CONC e subsequently married Shifra, daughter of Binyamin Wolf Spira-Wedeles and '''widow of Yitsḥak Bondy, the leader of one of Jewish Prague’s political factions''' [Not true!]    ''(Michael D. Bruell)''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.loebtree.com/oppdavid.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.loebtree.com/bondisi.html#sbs
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~prohel/names/loew/spira/spira.html#1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~prohel/names/loew/spira/spira.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Schifra (Shifra) SPIRA Born: bef 1673 Died: 31 Dec 1737 in Prague + R' Isaac ben Solomon ZALMAN (see BONDI family) Born: abt 1664 Occupation: rabbi of Prague 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Lawrence Weinberg has Schifra's husband as Salomon Lichtenstadt-Levi (bef 1678 m. 1691 - 1697 Prague) AND on Judaica Bohemiae: Salomon Oettingen Lichtenstadt, son of Abraham Aaron Lichtenstadt, had become engaged to Schifra,
2 CONC  the youngest daughter of R' Wolf Wedeles 
