1 NOTE {geni:about_me} the marriage of Jacob Heilbronn to Saul Bing's mother, the widow Roeslin, occurred before 1530. Saul and his wife Zirle appear in the Kanne at about that time. Roeslin (died after 1555 and probably after 1567) does
2 CONC  not have an Ele Toldot sheet of her own. She is just listed on the E. T. sheet for Jacob aus Heilbronn =um 1545, unfortunately, and ends up being one of several Roeslins who leave us fewer clues than we would like. She is almost 
2 CONC certainly from Bingen. We should also keep in mind that the "um 1538" death estimate for Saul is either completely incorrect (which is what we are hoping) or he died at a young age. In either case, Roeslin could have gone on livin
2 CONC g for many years after the last time she is seen by Ettlinger in records for the Kanne, i.e. 1567.
