1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is almost completely certain that the Rivke Serle http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-760 who is Meir haCohen’s daughter is not the one who is the widow of Loeb Oppenheim and wife or widow of 
2 CONC Amschel Storch. There are three reasons for this. First of all, it would be odd for her sons not to be receiving money from her estate until 1583 if she had died as early as January of 1579. Second, the description of Rivke Serle 
2 CONC on the gravestone certainly does not sound like it applies to a woman who had been married to two gaonim. Last, but most important, the name Meir is never used for any of her descendants, in spite of their being so many. Josef of 
2 CONC the weissen Loewen names a son Meir in honor of his father-in-law, but that is the only one, ever. The people who put Sorlin into Geni as the daughter of Meir haCohen were just reacting to a very iffy idea by Ettlinger where he wr
2 CONC ites, surrounded by question marks, that he wonders if that grave might be Sorlin’s. But everything we have seen since then points to it being someone else.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her Hebrew death date doesn't match up with the date of 23 January 1579
2 CONT
2 CONT Steinheim Institute has
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏ציון הלז שמתי לראש אשה חשובה והגונה מרת רבקה שערלן בת ר׳ מאיר הכהן ז״ל [נפטר׳ יום ו׳ כ״ו שבט של״ט לפ״ק תנצב״ה ׃]‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT Dieses Zeichen setzte ich zu Häupten einer Frau, angesehen und würdig, Frau Riwka Serlen, Tochter des Herrn Meir Hakohen, sein Andenken zum Segen, verschieden Tag 6, 26. Schwat 339 nach kleiner Zählung. Ihre Seele sei eingebunden 
2 CONC in das Bündel des Lebens
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-760&lang=en
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-177442812-2-500561/rebekka-riwka-sarah-sorle-serlen-oppenheimer-born-hakohencahen-katz-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-17d67465e36616da6e68ee3d6c418a6b
2 CONC &mrid=25c5d3fee286b442dfe6f8548e8bfeda MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 13 2018, 6:32:14 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The missing piece of the puzzle was always the question of HO 277's identity. Fine to say that she is not Sorlin, widow of Loeb Oppenheim, but much, much nicer to be able to say WHO she is.
2 CONT
2 CONT The answer has come from items #84-86 in the Frankfurt Pinkas, which show that Sorlin bat Meir had been married to Aberle of the Affe, by whom she had two sons, and that after Aberle's death in about 1572 she married Elieser bn Sh
2 CONC muel. They then lived in the Affe together, and he remained there after her death. (The Affe was a Wirtshaus, and he was the innkeeper there at that time, apparently, although Aberle, Sorlin's previous husband, had been identified
2 CONC  more as a Metzger/Fleischer, but probably was also the innkeeper. In addition, it should be noted that Elieser is the name of Aberle's father and also the name of one of Aberle's sons, as well as the name of Sorlin's second husba
2 CONC nd: 3 different Eliesers.)
2 CONT
2 CONT This Sorlin's marriage to Aberle occurred by 1560 (Ettlinger thinks they may have married about 1555), and they had at least Jacob (later called "Jacob Butter") and one other son (Elieser, whose name does not appear to be given in
2 CONC  the first two Pinkas records, but appears in the third one - #86 - dated 1617, as already deceased). In 1574 Sorlin makes a sworn statement regarding the amount of her dowry, in which she is called "Sara bat Meir z"l wittwe Abrah
2 CONC am bn Elieser". Her marriage to Elieser bn Shmuel probably occurred shortly after that, and she died a few years later, on 23 Jan 1579 (HO 277, Epidat ffb-760).
2 CONT
2 CONT Regarding the Sorlin who was married to Loeb Oppenheim of Worms and then to Amschel Cohen of the Storch in Frankfurt, she leaves only a couple of clues, but one of them is very helpful in narrowing down her death year range.  Alth
2 CONC ough Ettlinger carefully cites a record (Be.1583, page 90) which shows that her son Josef z weissen Loewen had recently inherited 1500 Florins, he does not state that the inheritance is specified as being from her: rather, he puts
2 CONC  "nach ihr" in parentheses, leaving us to trust that he knows from another source that it came from or through Sorlin. (And it should be noted that since we are hoping that Sorlin is a daughter of Saul Bing, and since Ettlinger gi
2 CONC ves the latter a death year estimate of "um 1582", this would fit perfectly, although it opens up a different issue.)
2 CONT
2 CONT But the clincher is that her son Suskind in Worms names a daughter Sorlin in her honor, and that Sorlin is already married by 1600.  So we can leave "um 1580" as the death estimate for Sorlin with the confidence that she at least 
2 CONC died in the first half of the 1580s.  She probably pre-deceased Amschel Storch, but either her gravestone did not survive in Frankfurt or she died while visiting a child or relative who lived elsewhere.
2 CONT
2 CONT In any case, she and HO 277 are two very different Sorlins.
