1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT Liwa Schuh Grotwol.	 A man was buried here	 upright and faithful, dear sir	 Josef Jehuda, son of	 Schlomo, his souvenir for blessing, various	 and bury day 2, 12.	 Ijar 392 after a small count
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments of Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died, Monday, May 3rd , 1632 Zln 1 and 4: Liwa a common name for Judah. Of the two first names, Josef Jehuda, as usual, the second is the "main name". Abbreviation check mark, sentence separator: '' in lines 2 and 5, which 
2 CONC lead to the formation of three sections: headers with name and formula, eulogy with religious name, and date of death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme with -man in lines 2/3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Headstone description Dimensions 72 x 57 x 18 cm Description flat-arched finish, Zl 1 in the arch. Condition Zl 6 partially and Zl 7 almost completely weathered.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Liwa lived in the Schuh house, he married his second wife Sorlen in 1621. From 1618 his name appeared in several files, in 1630 he had 8,000 guilders.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Schlomo S. Jizchak Schuh (No. ffb-0444 , Ho 410, ET 21.V.1607) Mother: Edel T. Josef Oppenheim (No. ffb-0421 , Ho 792, ET 2.XI.1654) wife I : Brajnle (No. ffb-2057 ?) Wife II: Sorlen from Eibelstadt T. Elj
2 CONC akim (Ho 5776 / no date, ET 23.X.1637) Son: Joswel Schuh (No. ffb-0404 , Ho 1360, ET 25 .XI.1695)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature sk, p. 88, no. 79 MF, p. 11, no. 16 (ET: 11-4) ET 3.V.1632 Dietz p. 270 Ho 607 HoNam p. 709: Grotwol Löw HoEd: Zl 2 טמון, in the text טמן. Zl 3 כמר, in the text כמ׳. HoSt 820
