2 CONT Metz Memorbuch #138 [English Translation]: The very learned and pious Rabbi Mordechai Israel son of Meir, "for he lived with piety all his life, always occupied himself with the study of the Law. He spread the Law in Israel and tr
2 CONC ained many noble students. He was for a long time a syndic, and led the community with gentleness, without ever irritating anyone. All his life he attended the synagogue, morning and evening, and sang the services with devotion an
2 CONC d a pleasant voice on the great feasts. His wife gave a gift to the hospice for him. Died immediately after he had finished the evening prayer, on Sunday 20 Tevet 400 [16 Jan 1640]. "He was known to all as Old Rabbi Zuskind". 
2 CONT
