1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memorbuch Entry #823 [English Translation]: The illustrious and worthy trustee of the community, Rabbi Ouri Faivouch Moses, son of Rabbi Gerson Cahen, who devoted himself to numerous interventions, went to the roya
2 CONC l court for the good of the community. He also went to the court of the Duke of Lorraine. He intervened for individuals. He was generous... and hospitable... he studied all his life and led the community with gentleness and righte
2 CONC ousness without pride or arrogance... he would have deserved that the presence of God was marked in him. He blew the shofar for more than thirty years, according to the Kabbalistic instructions. His sons made a donation to the hos
2 CONC pice for him. Died on Sunday and buried on Monday 4 Adar 5481 (3 Mar 1721)
2 CONT
2 CONT ML et GenAmi  p. 18
