1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: The master, Mr. Feibesch Bacharach. | Be witnessed that | 3 | here was hewn  a grave the great | Lord, perfect and ingenious in Torah, | and strengthened like a lion in the commandments, | 6 
2 CONC | the noble, the master, Mr. Josef Uri | Son of Moshe, his memory for blessing, different and bes | dig day 5, eve of new moon Sivan | 9 | 361 after a small count. His soul is part of the bundle of life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steinheim Institute Commentary: Dating Died, Thursday, May 31st, 1601 About the date: ET made a mistake in the date. His statement, May 19, 1601, a Shabbat, is not possible as a funeral. Ho had overlooked the line with the calenda
2 CONC r day when it was transcribed so that ET could not determine the exact date. The inscription is printed by Kaufmann. He specifies the year of death as 1701, which he corrects in the additions to Ho in 1601. Kaufmann, who published
2 CONC  his book in 1894, seven years before Ho published the inscriptions, still used it after the HoSt. orderly Ho manuscript. Kaufmann's rendition deviates from Ho a few times, for example in the name Feibesch, the merchant, as indica
2 CONC ted in the text with ?????, while Ho ?????? writes and in Zl 6 ?????, just like in the text while Ho ??? writes. We can therefore state that the Ho manuscript was still being edited before publication, although it was not only cor
2 CONC rected. His wife was buried next to Feibesch. Zl1 and 6: The name of the deceased Feibesch Bacharach forms the header. In the text, however, the religious name Josef Uri S. Mosche is mentioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Zl 2: cf. Gen 31.52; here the rhyme changes Zl 3/4: "perfect and ingenious" is said by a constant learner who not only masters the contents of the Torah well, but can also interpret it with acumen, cf. bHor 2b. Zl 5: cf. bPes 112
2 CONC a and others Zl 7/8: cross-line word. Abbreviation squiggles and double dashes; Sentence separator: dashes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme on -azaw in Zln 2/3 and on -e (a) we (a) r in Zln 3-5
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone description Dimensions 93 x 82 x 9 cm Description Rectangular stele with a double bevelled frame. The header is in the end. The title block ends trapezoidally. In lines 4 and 6, the last letter is partially or entirely o
2 CONC n the left frame. Condition Zl 8 and partially damaged.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Feibesch lived first in the red cock and then in the Bisemknopf, according to Dietz in the house Waage.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Mosche Bacharach (Ho 224, ET 8.X.1567) Mother: Fraidchen T. Elchanan died in 1577 (No. ffb-0536 , Ho 276, ET 1577/78) Wife: Sorlin T. Aharon Bonn (No. ffb- 0449 , Ho 804, ET 10.XII.1655) Children: Mosche (
2 CONC No. ffb-3749 , Ho 520, ET 25.IX.1624), Jachet (No. ffb-0471 , Ho 641, ET 6.IV.1636 ), Elle, d. before 1624 (not at Ho, ET b.19V.1601).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature Kaufmann, Bacharach, p. 17 note ET 19.V. 1601 Dietz p. 19 Ho 373 HoNam p. 698: Bacharach Feibesch Ho Ed: Zl 1 ??????, in the text ?????. Zl 2 ?????, as it would be correct, but ???? in the text of th
2 CONC e rhyme. Zl 6 ???, in the text ?????. Zl 7/8 prescriber ?????, in the text ?????. HoSt 989
