1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaak Isac etc. OPPENHEIM OPPENHEIMER: b. 1741, Fürth - d. 1781, Pressburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Also cf. information on son Ber Bernhard OPPENHEIMER.
2 CONT
2 CONT Particularly valuable details to be found in this fantastic piece:
2 CONT
2 CONT the Seforim blog: A Half Slave, Ber Oppenheimer, the Reliability of R’ Shlomo Sofer, and Other Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT http://seforim.blogspot.com/2017/06/a-half-slave-ber-oppenheimer.html?m=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracts:
2 CONT
2 CONT A Half Slave, Ber Oppenheimer, the Reliability of R’ Shlomo Sofer, and Other Comments By Brian Schwartz
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Ber Oppenheimer, a descendant of the famous R’ Dovid Oppenheim, was born in 1760 to his father Yitzchak in Pressburg. Together with his brother Chaim, young Ber went to study in the Yeshiva of Fürth. Sometime later, Oppenheimer le
2 CONC ft Fürth for Berlin so that he could fulfill his desire to learn secular knowledge. When he completed his studies in Berlin, he returned to Pressburg where he would become one of the leaders of the community.
2 CONT
2 CONT A few further details thanks to Jerusalem cousin Avraham who is kindly sharing biographical snippets with me that are contained in Bernhard OPPENHEIMER's 1829 book "Mei Be-er".
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that Isaak was born in Fürth and, because of his high opinion of the Yeshiva there, this is why he sent his two sons Baer & Chaim to study in that town at a young age. Bernhard recounts "his father giving them clear ins
2 CONC tructions as to how to conduct themselves and how to avoid the foolish behaviour of the other students they would encounter" He "credits his father for having set them on the correct path in life".
2 CONT
2 CONT Isak's wife is named here as "Raizel", the daughter of the "distinguished" Koppel DEUTSCH.
2 CONT
2 CONT This correlates relatively well with various sources that give her name as Sarla/Sara (Koppel) DEUTSCH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Such as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bluemle Oppenheim : Family tree by Peter FRIEDMANN - Geneanet
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/pfdm?lang=en&pz=israel&nz=fleischmann&ocz=1&p=bluemle&n=oppenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT 6-Rabbi Isaak OPPENHEIM (1741-1781), Rabbi of Pressburg married Sarla KOPPEL DEUTSCH (1736-1794)
