1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Bella bat Natan ⚭ Löb Staden [26.08.1704]  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=hha-1462&lang=de
2 CONT
2 CONT Her holy name (Bella bat Nathan) is known from her tombstone. We don't know her German name. In Yiddish her father's family name may be either Melrich or Me'elrich (i.e. from Elrich). According to Glückel, her mother was 44 years 
2 CONC old when her father died in 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT Glückel of Hameln wrote that after the plague of 1638 "My mother had already learned the trade of making gold and silver lace, and God in His mercy saw to it that she received orders from the Hamburg merchants. At first Jacob Ree,
2 CONC  of blessed memory, went surety for her; but when the merchants found that she knew her business and was prompt in her deliveries, they trusted her without surety. Next she taught the trade to a number of young girls and engaged t
2 CONC hem to work by her side, so that finally she was able to provide a living for her  mother and clean, decent clothes for herself. Little enough, however, remained over, and often my dear mother had nothing but a crust of bread the 
2 CONC livelong day” (Marvin Lowenthal, The Memoirs of Glückel of Hameln. New York: Schocken Books, 1977, p. 18).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Bela Melrich MP
2 CONT Gender: Female Birth: 1626 Death: August 26, 1704 (78)  Altona, now Hamburg, Germany Place of Burial: Altona, Germany Immediate Family: Daughter of Nathan Melrich and Mette (Mate) Nathans  Wife of Leib (Löb) Staden  Mother of Elke
2 CONC le Goldschmidt-Stadthagen; Hendel Pinkerle; Glückel von Hameln; Rebecca Riwka Pinkerle; Unknown Pinkerle; Mate Pinkerle and Abraham Benjamin Wolf Pinkerle « less  Sister of Loeb Mellrich; Mordechai Ellrich; Moses Melrich??; Glücke
2 CONC l Ellrich and Olga Ulrike Ulke Kohen  Added by: Avraham Samson on January 1, 2008 Managed by: Eve Cohen (Picard) and 15 others Curated by: Simon Goodman
2 CONT
2 CONT Her holy name (Bella bat Nathan) is known from her tombstone. We don't know her German name. In Yiddish her father's family name may be either Melrich or Me'elrich (i.e. from Elrich). According to Glückel, her mother was 44 years 
2 CONC old when her father died in 1670. Glückel of Hameln wrote that after the plague of 1638 "My mother had already learned the trade of making gold and silver lace, and God in His mercy saw to it that she received orders from the Hamb
2 CONC urg merchants. At first Jacob Ree, of blessed memory, went surety for her; but when the merchants found that she knew her business and was prompt in her deliveries, they trusted her without surety. Next she taught the trade to a n
2 CONC umber of young girls and engaged them to work by her side, so that finally she was able to provide a living for her mother and clean, decent clothes for herself. Little enough, however, remained over, and often my dear mother had 
2 CONC nothing but a crust of bread the livelong day” (Marvin Lowenthal, The Memoirs of Glückel of Hameln. New York: Schocken Books, 1977, p. 18).
2 CONT
