2 CONT
2 CONT Physician in Orlëans.  Cured Count Etampes of gout.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Flourished about 1360-1370. He probably lived in Erfurt during the French expulsion of Jews between 1322 1359.
2 CONT
2 CONT (from Ma'alot HaYochasin).
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an oral tradition that Rashi's son-in-law adopted the surname of Lurie from the Hebrew phrase "Le-Or-Yah" (by G-d's light). Jewish genealogists have recognized the Lurie (or Luria) family as having traced its genealogy ba
2 CONC ck to the 10th century B.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Lurie Legacy", Neil Rosenstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to others the surname "Luria", maybe originated from settling in the town of Loria west of Bassano in the Vicensa district in Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Dr. Paul Jacobi, "The Historicity of the RaSHI Descent", Avotaynu, vol VI No. 1 p 23] 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://barkai-family.com/Documents/Family%20Tree%201.jpg
2 CONT
