1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Saul’s stepfather, Jacob Heilbronn =um 1545, is an important man and, interestingly, is the brother-in-law and business partner of Meir Weissenberg, who, has some connections to Bingen.  Jacob had come from Heilbro
2 CONC nn around 1513 to marry Gute, daughter of Salomon Nuernberg zur Kanne (=um 1513, possibly Epidat ffb-3378). We don't know if Jacob and Gute had any children together, but the "son-in-law of Jacob" who is mentioned in Andernacht2 #
2 CONC 771 in April, 1547, has not yet been identified, and this may indicate that Jacob and Gute had a daughter. This record also shows (as do a couple of others cited by Ettlinger) that Jacob was still alive in 1547.
