1 NAME Brinlen bat Günzberg
2 GIVN Brinlen bat Günzberg
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 ADR1  Battonnstraße
3 CITY Frankfurt Am Main
3 STAE HE
3 POST 60311
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 16 OCT 1612
2 ADDR
3 CITY Frankfurt Am Main
3 STAE HE
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: Breinlen Günzburg, wife of the Liwa to the shoe	 Here is a woman buried, respected and worthy, woman Breinlen, daughter of the Torah scholar, Mr. Schlomo, have a lot of good days, Amen, she w
2 CONC as buried on day 3, 18 Tishri year 373 of the small count. Your soul is part of the bundle of life, Amen Sela
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments by Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died, Sunday, October 14th, 1612 (?) Zl 1: Günzburg, about Guinzburg written; Schuh, about schuch written. Zl 6: See Spr 3.1; a formula that is added after the name of the living. Abbreviation Tilde ?; Sentence separator: h
2 CONC alf-high diamond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme on -nah in Zln 3/4.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone description Dimensions 74 x 85 x 15 cm Description Stele with a rounded arch, the recessed lettering field is also rounded. In the upper right, in a recessed round, the house sign, raised. House sign shoe condition The s
2 CONC tone is partially sunken, the two lower visible lines are partially weathered.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Brinlen was a daughter of Schlomo Ulm-Günzburg, the seventh son of the famous Schimon Günzburg. The year of Schlomo's death is unknown. He died of a 25th Elul after 1612, because Breinlen's inscription shows that 
2 CONC he was still alive when she died. The exact date of Breinlen's death is also not entirely clear. The date is incorrect for שע״ג (1612) in the Ho copy. Lö writes (Günzburg ...) that she died in October 1612. information that presum
2 CONC ably comes from Ho (because Lö points to his Günzburg in his Jewish tombstones. He also noted the inconsistency of the date at Ho), although Ho had not copied the inscription's Zl 1, which is very important for the data. Because o
2 CONC f Ho's omission, ET could not match Breinlen and even suspects that she was not married. In a remark by ET regarding his entry Liwa Schuh, Breinlen's husband, he wrote: "Li1619 (referring to the year 1619?) Has the married couple 
2 CONC Löb and Bräunle in the shoe", which means our Breinlen. In 1621 Liwa married Sorlen from Eibelstadt. Perhaps this information indicates that Breinlen had died a few years after 1612. Breinlen (HoSt 2404) is buried next to her sist
2 CONC er Zürle G. Jaakow Günzburg (No. ffb-2056 , Ho 393, HoSt 2406, ET 21.II.1604).
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Schlomo Günzburg Mother: unknown Husband: Liwa for the shoe S. Schlomo Grotwol (No. ffb-0423 , Ho 607, ET 3.V.1632) Child (?): Josef (No. ffb-0404 , Ho 1360, ET 25.XI.1695).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature Lö, Günzburg and the Swabian communities, in: Blätter ..., II. Jg., No. 4, p. 27 ET 14.X.1612 (?) Dietz, p. 270 (mentions the husband) Lö, Jewish gravestones , in: Blätter ..., II. Jg., No. 8, p. 60 
2 CONC Ho 456 HoNam p. 700: Breinle T. Salomon HoEd: Zl 1 is missing for Ho. Zln 7/8 the date for Ho is not correct , a check is not possible because the stone has sunk. HoSt 2404
