1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: The sublime elderly, honored Mr. Joswel Schuh,	 different at night and buried on day 6, 18. Kislev 456 after a small count that his soul was integrated into the bundle of life. I put this sto
2 CONC ne on Heads of an upright and faithful man, he was known for all good works riding, his acting and walking was in faithfulness at any time and season, the dear, dear sir joseph, son of josef yehuda,
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary by Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died, Thursday, November 24th, 1695 The sk announces that "2 shoes off the feet (from Joswel) to the east stood the tomb of his father". Today the tombs are about 4m apart. Zl 1: Extension of the name with שוך (shoe), after
2 CONC  MF and sk. The specification שור (Schur) at Ho was not adopted. Zln 2/3: The time of death was "at night 6". The sk writes "and buried the next day, day 6", from which we can conclude that Joswel died on Thursday. The day of the 
2 CONC month with chai-alive instead of 18 as turning away from the negative. Zl 4: Gen 28,22 Zln 6 / 7a: cf. bBQ 38b, probably cross-line word. Zln7/8: cf. bShab 31a Abbreviation apostrophe and dots; Sentence separator: no
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme with -na 5,7 and 8
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone description Dimensions 112 x 86 x 12 cm Condition Canceled in and below Zl 8. Part of the arch lies in front of the stone. The title block is badly damaged.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Joswel lived in the front building Schuh. The MF emphasizes its regular prayer.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Liwa Schuh-Grotwol (No. ffb-0423 , Ho 607, ET 3.V.1632) Mother: unknown Wife: Minkle T. Jizchak Haas (No. ffb-0141 , 1419, ET 27.IV.1700) children : Schlome (Ho 1767, ET 1.II.1721), Herts, who died before 
2 CONC 1700, Gitche G. Gedalja SeGaL zum Korb (ET 11.IX.1737, not with Ho) and Sorlen (Ho 1189, ET 11.II .1686).
