1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Back again, now.  If the hint that Karl is brother to Gumperz Wetzlar of Hanau is correct, then here is Gumperz:  He is (Mordechai) Gumprich Wetzlar, a physician, and he dies in Hanau (per Lagis-Hessen) 2 IX 1794 (
2 CONC 2/3 September being the favorite death date in the family, apparently). Two of his daughters die in Hanau, but one, Fanny Fradche, is HO 5562 and dies 13 III 1827 as widow of Moses Kulp bn Juda and current wife of Siegmund Geisenh
2 CONC eimer aus Bingen. Everything points to Dr. Gumperz/Gumprich being a son of Loeb Wetzlar of Hanau bn Josel, but the father's name is not shown on his tombstone. This is, however, the only Wetzlar family with connections to both Han
2 CONC au and Offenbach, so the birthplace of Karl as Offenbach does lend strength to the theory.
