2 _MARNM Model
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1760
2 PLAC Harburg
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamburg
3 STAE Hamburg
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Court Jew in Ansbach + Pfalz-Neuburg + Wallerstein 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Court Jew in Ansbach + Pfalz-Neuburg + Wallerstein got free pass for Pfalz-Neuburg in 1755 1712-20 built splendid residence in Monheim - expelled 1741 - died 1760 in Harburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT Model came from a family of Jewish court factors the Margrave of Ansbach. He was the grandson of Marx Model in Ansbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1730 he had a residential and commercial building with rich furnishings in a central location in Monheim built, which today as city hall is used.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1739 the model was the Prince of Oettingen-Wallerstein for many years of useful service named "Cabinets and Cammer Factor". He was thus in all stately shops in preference to any competitor. Model Oettingischen was at the Counts
2 CONC  Fayencenmanufaktur involved, where he lost a lot of money in the unsuccessful companies.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1741 could be model for the expulsion of the Jews from Monheim in Harburg, where he died poor 1760th
